    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0586" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/2803: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-28T12:00:00-03:00">February 28,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 4—1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–345. President Vargas has personally brought following to my attention with
                    request for good offices:</p>
                <p>Within the next few days he will instruct his Ambassador in Washington to apply
                    for some 3000 to 3500 trucks under Lend-lease. He explained to me that the
                    transportation system of the country is critical and that these trucks are
                    urgently needed not only for the Army but also to move foodstuffs, etc., from
                    the interior.</p>
                <p>I told the President that I would transmit this information to the
                    Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
